1
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:23,940
♪Her smile, her kindness, her kiss♪

2
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:25,820
♪Her presumptions♪

3
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,300
♪She was in love, she was tired, she walked away♪

4
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,660
♪Only tears remained♪

5
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:36,180
♪Can't hold on, can't forget♪

6
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:39,500
♪Can't let go of her all-or-nothing love♪

7
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,100
♪Promises became a burden after all that hesitation♪

8
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:47,500
♪Leaving longing frozen into a winter night♪

9
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:53,420
♪That girl, my girl♪

10
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:57,540
♪The light's still on, but you're already far away♪

11
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:01,020
♪The words reach my lips, but I can't get them out♪

12
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:06,740
♪That girl, my girl♪

13
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:10,860
♪My voice echoes, but no one answers♪

14
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:14,340
♪Is this really how it ends for us?♪

15
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,980
[You don't have to be perfect tobe worthy of Love]

16
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:35,380
[The Early Spring]

17
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:37,940
[Adapted from The Early Spring on jjwxc.net, Author: Gu Niang Bie Ku]

18
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:12,620
[Episode 2]
[The Workplace Isn't Some Kind of Child's Play]

19
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,710
Help!

20
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:40,950
Let me open the door.

21
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,840
Sorry.

22
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:50,120
It's all my fault.

23
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,280
I was taking a shower and didn't hear my phone ring.

24
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,680
The landlord told me

25
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,560
a new tenant would be coming tonight.

26
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,310
I forgot to inform Tao

27
00:02:57,630 --> 00:02:59,190
and caused her to mistake you for some hooligan.

28
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:00,620
Sorry.

29
00:03:01,030 --> 00:03:02,190
It's my fault.

30
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:04,630
I should've waited for her to enter the house before coming up.

31
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,120
Actually, I could feel that you were scared,

32
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,400
so I didn't enter the lift.

33
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,520
I didn't expect

34
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:10,840
that I would still scare you.

35
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:11,910
Sorry.

36
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:12,630
That's not it.

37
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,360
I was way too timid.

38
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:16,190
I probably scared you too.

39
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:17,030
I even

40
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,000
broke two bottles of your sauce.

41
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:20,520
It's fine.

42
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,910
Well,

43
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,960
I am Sun Yuanzhu.

44
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,400
Sun Yu.

45
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,000
Hello.

46
00:03:31,630 --> 00:03:32,710
Shang Zhitao.

47
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,560
Hello.

48
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,410
It's normal to have a boy as a flatmate in Beijing.

49
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:40,430
Don't worry.

50
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:42,630
I'll interrogate him later.

51
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,870
Wow.

52
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:48,030
You have so many types of seasoning.

53
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:49,000
You can cook too?

54
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:50,740
Just simple meals.

55
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:52,140
I'll make something for you two if I get the chance.

56
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:54,170
That's exactly what I'm waiting for.

57
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:55,630
Do you need any help?

58
00:03:56,430 --> 00:03:56,980
No need.

59
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:01,630
Do you work at BAT?

60
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,240
Yes. I work in the IT industry.

61
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:07,520
A rising star in the tech industry.

62
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,680
I work for an online dating company.

63
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,750
Find me if you need anything.

64
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:11,310
Sure.

65
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:13,660
Tao.

66
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,900
An advertising elite working in Lime.

67
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:17,360
Lime?

68
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:18,510
Lime is amazing.

69
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,510
Those who work there are all incredible.

70
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:20,300
Not at all.

71
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,600
I just got hired.

72
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,780
Just a rookie.

73
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,960
When you've survived the initial phase,

74
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:27,500
you'll be a proven elite.

75
00:04:27,950 --> 00:04:29,080
When I started working,

76
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:32,070
I spent a whole night at the convenience store entrance editing my slides.

77
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,390
I was even mistaken for an oden thief.

78
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,040
An oden thief?

79
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:38,540
What was your name again?

80
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,520
Zhu.

81
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,020
Sun Yuanzhu.

82
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:44,880
Sun Yuanzhu.

83
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,190
Sorry.

84
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:48,630
Is your name from the poem

85
00:04:49,190 --> 00:04:50,390
"My lofty aspirations encompass the world;

86
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:52,040
My wings yearn to carry me to far-off heights?"

87
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:55,360
You actually know the poem?

88
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,120
My father taught it to me when I was young.

89
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,390
That's amazing.

90
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:00,680
I hereby announce

91
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,920
the completion of our temporary

92
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,240
three-man home.

93
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,750
It's late. Get your things sorted

94
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:06,920
and go to bed when you're done.

95
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,800
Tomorrow is Saturday.

96
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:08,750
Let's talk after we wake up.

97
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,390
Sure.

98
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:10,240
Good night.

99
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:13,510
After you.

100
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,390
After you.

101
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:16,950
After you.

102
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:19,630
I'll go in first.

103
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:20,630
Sorry.

104
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:24,870
After her.

105
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:46,660
Boss.

106
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,240
We lost the Qipai project.

107
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:53,070
Mr. Lin handed the project to Alex.

108
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,000
What?

109
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,680
Our project has been taken away by Division Two.

110
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:03,680
Boss, are you listening?

111
00:06:03,870 --> 00:06:05,680
He agreed to the 30% discount and signed the contract?

112
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,000
I guess.

113
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,560
What an embarrassment.

114
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,000
I've embarrassed you.

115
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:14,530
I mean, Alex

116
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:15,760
is an embarrassment to Lime.

117
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:16,920
Exactly.

118
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:18,120
You've spent years

119
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,870
maintaining Qipai as a client.

120
00:06:19,870 --> 00:06:21,240
We made the proposal

121
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,430
after staying up late for half a month.

122
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,560
Now, the project has been taken away from our hands.

123
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,040
Boss.

124
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,510
What should we do now?

125
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,800
If we can't

126
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,000
complete this month's KPI,

127
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,920
- we will... - Look.

128
00:06:31,510 --> 00:06:32,510
Go and accept

129
00:06:32,510 --> 00:06:33,920
the Mulanshuo e-commerce project.

130
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,510
Didn't you say to reject it?

131
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:38,360
That company has all kinds of issues.

132
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:40,360
They are even requesting a specific production team.

133
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,600
Great.

134
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,680
I hope you have other alternatives.

135
00:06:53,510 --> 00:06:55,120
Which production team has the client requested?

136
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,160
Laiyu,

137
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:57,920
a production team in Guangzhou.

138
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,160
They have a new energy vehicle commercial

139
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:01,000
that went viral in the first half of the year.

140
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,600
They are quite popular among the southern media outlets.

141
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,430
They are not bad.

142
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,560
Have you contacted them?

143
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,270
I have.

144
00:07:05,270 --> 00:07:06,510
They are very interested in working with us,

145
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:08,600
but their whole team is based in Guangzhou.

146
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,830
Give me the team's profile.

147
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:12,160
- Sure. - I'll leave the rest to you.

148
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:12,720
Sure.

149
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:13,720
Boss.

150
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:17,160
All the other employees are working on other projects.

151
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,600
Can I bring Shang Zhitao along

152
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,270
for this project?

153
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,600
She is patient and has a good temper.

154
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:23,720
No one else

155
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:26,270
in Lime is better than her at this.

156
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,560
Luke.

157
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:30,360
I won't quit.

158
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,190
Go ahead.

159
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,040
I also think she'll be helpful.

160
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:35,680
Helpful?

161
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:37,430
Honest

162
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:38,360
and single-minded.

163
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,720
How long will she last in the advertising industry?

164
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:45,680
Didn't you tell me

165
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,000
to go ahead?

166
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:56,420
[20,300 yuan has been deposited]

167
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:04,160
Mom.

168
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:05,270
Tao.

169
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,270
I transferred 16,000 yuan to you.

170
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:09,240
Did you receive it?

171
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,270
Are you sure it's 16,000 yuan?

172
00:08:11,270 --> 00:08:12,360
Why did I receive

173
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,270
20,300 yuan instead?

174
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:15,920
Did the bank give me extra?

175
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,310
When I told your dad

176
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:19,120
to transfer you some money,

177
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,430
he didn't even hesitate.

178
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,680
He would give you a gold mine if he had one,

179
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,750
let alone the little bit of money he has now.

180
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,360
Why didn't you give us a call

181
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,680
after you arrived?

182
00:08:28,870 --> 00:08:30,360
How are your food and accommodation?

183
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,600
Do you have enough money?

184
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,670
Which question should I answer first?

185
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:37,790
Calm down.

186
00:08:37,790 --> 00:08:39,240
You can find a job slowly

187
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:41,000
until you find the right one.

188
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,270
Don't make do with your job.

189
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:43,360
If you can't find one, come home.

190
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,360
We'll support you.

191
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,000
Coming home is also a good choice.

192
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:49,550
Mom. Dad. I love you both so much.

193
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:51,000
Don't worry, both of you.

194
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:53,440
Your daughter has been impressive.

195
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:56,120
I'm now working at the biggest advertising company in China.

196
00:08:56,270 --> 00:08:59,910
Of course, my daughter is impressive.

197
00:08:59,910 --> 00:09:02,270
You joined a large company in Beijing as soon as you graduated.

198
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:04,120
Their revenue reaches billions of yuan.

199
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,840
I'm telling you.

200
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:05,720
The ancestors

201
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,720
of the Shang family

202
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:09,150
are more than proud of you.

203
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,240
Do you think an ordinary person is good enough for you?

204
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,080
No.

205
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,390
Absolutely not.

206
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,510
I have to go now.

207
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:16,510
My superior is looking for me.

208
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,000
Don't be too exhausted from working.

209
00:09:19,510 --> 00:09:21,510
If your superior dares to bully you,

210
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:23,030
your mother and I will fly over

211
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:24,030
to protect you with sticks in our hands.

212
00:09:24,030 --> 00:09:25,030
Got it.

213
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:25,720
I'm hanging up.

214
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:27,720
You're already...

215
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,120
She hung up.

216
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:32,270
Tao,

217
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:33,510
pack up.

218
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:34,510
We are going on a business trip.

219
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:35,670
We leave tomorrow morning.

220
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,120
Okay.

221
00:09:41,510 --> 00:09:42,270
Come in.

222
00:09:47,510 --> 00:09:48,840
Came to the office on a weekend?

223
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,440
It's rare for you to do that.

224
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:54,320
Alex's group stole your client, Qipai.

225
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:56,120
They're having a celebration dinner tonight.

226
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,670
They asked me to come over and arrange it.

227
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:00,120
They sell ideas as if they were street vendors.

228
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:01,670
I suggest you send their group

229
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:02,930
to the market.

230
00:10:04,550 --> 00:10:06,510
It's not a bad idea.

231
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,320
I'll try to contact the market later.

232
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:11,200
Speaking of which,

233
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:12,840
in three months,

234
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,720
the company will appoint one of you two directors

235
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,360
as the acting general manager.

236
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:18,960
Sales KPI

237
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,600
is the most important assessment criterion.

238
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,960
I think

239
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,200
he probably has heard something about it.

240
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,510
Otherwise, he wouldn't have

241
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:28,120
dared to slash his price to steal your client.

242
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:30,080
I wish him success, then.

243
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:36,870
Look at this.

244
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:41,360
[Mulanshuo E-commerce TVC proposal]

245
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,310
[Business Division One]
Mulanshuo?

246
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,870
No wonder you are so calm.

247
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:48,240
Turns out, you've taken the Mulanshuo project.

248
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,120
However, their budget

249
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:52,480
is 20% higher than Qipai's.

250
00:10:52,790 --> 00:10:54,240
This is a huge project.

251
00:10:55,270 --> 00:10:56,600
I'm sure Lumi will be very busy.

252
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:57,630
Oh,

253
00:10:57,630 --> 00:10:59,600
is she getting Shang Zhitao involved in the project, as well?

254
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:01,120
If you really care about her,

255
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,080
spare her some manpower.

256
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,360
It's urgent, and the workload is heavy.

257
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:06,080
A rookie won't be much help.

258
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,510
Got it.

259
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:09,080
When you're shooting the commercial,

260
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,000
I'll assign some people to help you.

261
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:14,720
Fine. I won't disturb you any longer.

262
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:16,750
I'll go contact the supermarket now.

263
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:18,960
I'm leaving.

264
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:24,820
[1.2 Core Competitiveness]

265
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:26,440
[2.1 Main Creative Team (1) Director: Li Wencai]

266
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,940
[(2) Main Outdoor Photography: Pan Weihao]

267
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:42,390
What time is your flight tomorrow?

268
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,060
Help me book a ticket.

269
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:56,100
[Guangzhou]

270
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,750
Flora.

271
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,360
You're so early.

272
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:07,840
Are you studying?

273
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:08,840
I'm just reading.

274
00:12:09,510 --> 00:12:10,650
Luke, good morning.

275
00:12:11,670 --> 00:12:12,170
Morning.

276
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:14,630
Do you want coffee?

277
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:15,600
I'm going to buy coffee.

278
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,600
Let me pay for it.

279
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,360
No need.

280
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:20,630
Don't try to use any street smarts.

281
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:21,960
It doesn't suit you.

282
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:34,030
This boss of mine

283
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,630
is handsome,

284
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,870
but he has a foul mouth.

285
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,860
[Guangzhou]

286
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,600
This is already the fourth brew.

287
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,360
- I'm going to order some liquor. - Thank you.

288
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,240
What's the meaning of this?

289
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,510
They said they were already on the way an hour ago.

290
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,310
Fooling around with me?

291
00:12:58,510 --> 00:12:59,240
Calm down.

292
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,750
Calm down, you say?

293
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,720
Mr. Li.

294
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:17,630
It's been a while.

295
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,510
I didn't expect

296
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,960
you to come in person.

297
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:24,960
When I saw your name,

298
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:25,960
I wanted to pay you a visit.

299
00:13:29,750 --> 00:13:30,840
Do you two know each other?

300
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:31,600
We do.

301
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:35,360
Luke is our team's benefactor.

302
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,510
Mr. Li, you flatter me.

303
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,120
Don't be so humble.

304
00:13:39,630 --> 00:13:40,630
Four years ago,

305
00:13:40,630 --> 00:13:42,720
if you hadn't kicked us out of the project,

306
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:45,360
our team wouldn't have achieved so many things now.

307
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,630
Don't bully a young person for being poor,

308
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:49,960
for he might turn into a dragon one day.

309
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:52,240
Don't believe it, and you'll be poor forever.

310
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,080
This has been our team's motto

311
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,720
for all these years.

312
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,360
I can't believe

313
00:13:57,750 --> 00:13:59,600
I get to say it to you today.

314
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,360
I didn't look down on your team back then.

315
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,750
It's only a given

316
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:07,200
for you to achieve great things today.

317
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,600
Even if I could turn back time,

318
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:11,360
after much deliberation,

319
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,630
your team still wouldn't necessarily be the best choice.

320
00:14:14,870 --> 00:14:16,000
I completely understand.

321
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,830
So, our team also did much deliberation

322
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:20,510
regarding your project today.

323
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,750
The project is not bad,

324
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,120
and the budget is high.

325
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,360
However, our team can't fit this project into our schedule.

326
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:27,870
Please find another team

327
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:29,960
